Anyone would think you don't like pets. Actually, I just want a pet
dragon. Nothing more. 
Seriously though, it is my experience that it is annoying to control
one pet let alone several. For instance you have to be more careful
of where you step and getting equipment is harder, since pet A picks
up the two-handed sword, then drops it, just before I reach it, pet
B picks it up and so on. Before you had an option of having several 
pets instead of one. Now you don't. Kind of funny though, imaging a whole
group of hardened warriors just chasing a little kitten.

The system will also have to have alot more food (and other stuff) 
to support not only the warriors, but their little pets.

Which leads onto the next point, what happens when the pet dies?
Will the gods be slightly angry with one character or the whole group.
What happens when a god is totally pissed off with his character?
Does the lightning bolt just zap the character or the whole group?
What happens when the god wants to reward? Is it only one character
or a group (since it must have been a group effort)?
Will the group support the same god (not true to life) or do
they each have their own deities? If it is the latter, wouldn't it
make it an interesting system if members of the same group support
opposing gods (i.e. one supports Thor, the other Loki)? Does he/she
get rewarded by the god if he/she kills the other member. What about
actually sacrificing the other member (gosh, what a blood-thirsty game)
Must do wonders to the morale of the group. Who gets based on the sacrifices
made. If a person sacrifices something, does this mean the less a group
has to sacrifice before they get something or just that person?

